<% content_for :head do %>
  <% set_meta_tags(
    title: "Custom Fintech Software Development",
    description: "Marketplace payouts, earned wage access, payment processor migrations and Stripe Connect platforms, built with ledger-first accounting and audit trails.",
    keywords: "fintech software development partner, financial services automation, fintech software development, payment orchestration, split payments, automated settlements, earned wage access, Stripe Connect"
  ) %>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  <%= raw({
    "@context" => "https://schema.org",
    "@type" => "Service",
    "name" => "Custom Fintech Software Development",
    "url" => industry_financial_url,
    "description" => "Marketplace payouts, earned wage access, payment processor migrations and Stripe Connect platforms, built with ledger-first accounting and audit trails.",
    "provider" => { "@id" => "https://astechware.com/#organization" },
    "areaServed" => ["United States", "United Kingdom", "Canada", "Australia"],
    "serviceType" => "Fintech Engineering",
    "category" => "Financial Technology"
  }.to_json) %>
  </script>
<% end %>

<div class="hero-section py-5 service-page-hero financial-hero industry-landing-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center min-vh-50">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-9 mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3" data-page-h1>
          Custom fintech software development
        </h1>
        <p class="text-white fw-semibold mb-3" style="max-width: 720px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto">
          High Security Platforms for Payments, Lending, and Automated Settlements
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4" style="max-width: 800px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95)">
          We build production ready payment and settlement systems for marketplaces, payroll apps, and booking platforms. Ledger first accounting, idempotent money movement, and audit trails that hold up when webhooks arrive out of order.
        </p>
        <a href="https://calendly.com/ahmadkamran/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg rounded-pill px-5">
          Book a 30-min call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="inner-sections financial-industry-page">

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="what-we-do">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">What we actually do</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-4">
            Most payment products fall apart at one of three places: a split that drifts when a webhook retries, a ledger that cannot explain where money went, or a processor migration that leaves half the tenants on the old stack. We build systems where none of those failures are possible by design, not by policy.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-5">
            We focus on a narrow slice of fintech work where we have shipped production systems:
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Marketplace payouts and split payments</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Multi party flows where one charge becomes several ledgered balances, then payouts, with deterministic fee rules and idempotent execution so retries never double pay.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Earned wage access and payroll settlement</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Accrual engines that compute safe to withdraw limits from attendance and payroll data, disburse advances, and settle automatically against employer banking files.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Booking platforms that take payments</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              High concurrency booking with card present and online payments, POS sync, and tenant isolated financial records that survive peak traffic without double charges.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Payment processor and POS integrations</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Stripe Connect, Stripe Terminal, Clover, and Square integrations for platforms that need online and card present rails without reinventing reconciliation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row mt-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <p class="large-para mb-0 text-muted">
            If your build doesn&rsquo;t fit one of these, we will tell you on the first call.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="principles">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-3 pb-3 d-inline-block">How we think about fintech builds</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">A few principles that show up in every system we ship.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 h-100">
            <h3 class="h6 mb-2">Ledger first, bank second</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">Every charge produces ledger entries before money moves. Virtual balances reconcile before payouts fire. Month end becomes an audit step, not a fire drill.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 h-100">
            <h3 class="h6 mb-2">Idempotency is not optional</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">Webhooks arrive out of order. Retries happen. Partial outages are normal. Unique keys on every money moving request make duplicate charges and split errors structurally rare.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 h-100">
            <h3 class="h6 mb-2">Deterministic money, AI for explanation</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">Where we use AI next to financial numbers, Python calculates the figures with fixed formulas. The model explains; it never invents an offer price or a fee.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 h-100">
            <h3 class="h6 mb-2">Designed to support PCI DSS and SOC 2</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">We design payment systems to support PCI DSS and SOC 2 requirements. We do not claim certification we have not earned.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 h-100">
            <h3 class="h6 mb-2">Tenant isolation on financial data</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">Multi tenant platforms isolate each tenant&rsquo;s financial records so one customer&rsquo;s ledger, payouts, and settlement files cannot leak into another.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 h-100">
            <h3 class="h6 mb-2">Audit trails that answer who moved what</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">Every state change on money paths records actor, timestamp, action, and prior value. If a charge looks wrong six months later, the path is reconstructable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="spotlights">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-3 pb-3 d-inline-block">Case studies</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">Real payment and settlement work we have shipped.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Zofi cash: earned wage access platform</h3>
            <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Full stack EWA ecosystem that calculates earned but unpaid wages in real time, sets a safe to withdraw limit, disburses advances, and settles automatically via employer banking files. Built for payroll correctness under time corrections and payout failures.
            </p>
            <%= link_to "Read the full case study &rarr;".html_safe, case_study_path("zofi-cash-fintech"), class: "d-inline-block mt-4 fw-semibold ajax" %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Vestra: multi party payment orchestration</h3>
            <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              PropTech marketplace payment layer that splits rent between owners, maintenance reserves, and platform fees at the point of transaction. Double entry ledger, Stripe Connect, and idempotent execution so month end is not a manual reconciliation exercise.
            </p>
            <%= link_to "Read the full case study &rarr;".html_safe, case_study_path("vestra-payments"), class: "d-inline-block mt-4 fw-semibold ajax" %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">GolfPay360: booking payments and POS</h3>
            <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Multi tenant golf booking platform with Stripe Terminal for card present payments and Clover and Square POS SDKs, plus distributed locking so tee time drops do not double book or double charge.
            </p>
            <%= link_to "Read the full case study &rarr;".html_safe, case_study_path("golfpay360-saas"), class: "d-inline-block mt-4 fw-semibold ajax" %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">AI real estate deal analyzer</h3>
            <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Address in, investment analysis out: ARV, exit strategies, recommended offer, and a plain English explanation. Python owns every number; Claude explains them. No hallucinated offer prices.
            </p>
            <%= link_to "Read the full case study &rarr;".html_safe, case_study_path("ai-deal-analyzer"), class: "d-inline-block mt-4 fw-semibold ajax" %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <% if route_helper_defined?(:integration_path) %>
        <div class="row mt-4">
          <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
            <p class="mb-2">
              <%= link_to "Stripe integration →", integration_path("stripe"), class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
              <%= link_to "Payment gateway migration →", integration_path("payment-gateway-migration"), class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="who-we-work-with">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">Who we work with</h2>
          <ul class="mb-0 ps-3 large-para" style="line-height: 2;">
            <li>Marketplaces that need to split payments across multiple parties</li>
            <li>Earned wage access and payroll apps that settle advances against employer payroll</li>
            <li>Booking platforms taking online and card present payments, and companies integrating or migrating payment processors</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="engage">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">How we engage</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-4">
            We start every fintech engagement with a paid one week scoping call. You get a written deliverable you own whether or not you continue with us:
          </p>
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 mb-4">
            <ul class="mb-0 ps-3" style="line-height: 2;">
              <li>A money flow map of your proposed or existing system, with every charge, split, and payout path identified</li>
              <li>A risk register covering ledger correctness, idempotency, webhook failure modes, and audit defensibility</li>
              <li>An architecture recommendation with processor selection, ledger design, and integration approach</li>
              <li>A phased build plan with milestones</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <a href="https://calendly.com/ahmadkamran/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg rounded-pill px-5">
              Book a 30-min call
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "blogs/niche_guides", category_slug: "fintech" %>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-3 pb-3 d-inline-block">FAQ</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <div class="accordion financial-industry-faq" id="financialIndustryFaq">
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#finfaq1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="finfaq1">Are you PCI DSS or SOC 2 certified?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="finfaq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#financialIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">We design payment systems to support PCI DSS and SOC 2 requirements. We do not claim to be certified. If your engagement requires a formal attestation path, we design the architecture and evidence collection accordingly and work with your auditor.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#finfaq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="finfaq2">Which payment processors have you integrated?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="finfaq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#financialIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">We have shipped Stripe Connect for marketplace splits, Stripe Terminal for card present payments, and Clover and Square POS SDKs on booking platforms. Processor choice depends on your rails, not a preferred vendor list.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#finfaq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="finfaq3">Do you build for banks or crypto?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="finfaq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#financialIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Our shipped fintech work is marketplaces, earned wage access, booking payments, and processor integrations. We do not claim neobank, crypto exchange, or core banking experience we have not shipped.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#finfaq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="finfaq4">Do you offer ongoing maintenance?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="finfaq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#financialIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. Most fintech clients move to a monthly retainer after the initial build for monitoring, processor updates, reconciliation support, and feature work. We do not take on money moving builds without a clear post launch support plan.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "shared/hire_cta" %>

</div>
